                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How is Chennai's skincare market different from Mumbai + Delhi?</h3>
                                        <p>South Indian heritage + Tamil + Malayalam creative + Ayurveda + herbal + traditional preferences + Akshaya Tritiya + Onam + Pongal + Diwali festive calendar. Distinct from North + West India preferences.</p>
                                        <h3>What makes Kolkata + Bengali skincare marketing distinct?</h3>
                                        <p>Bengali traditional + regional-cultural + gifting + festive-heavy. Durga Puja + Poila Boishakh + wedding-gifting-driven. Bengali + English + Hindi creative needs. Growing D2C ecosystem.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need Tamil + Bengali + Telugu creative for South + East India?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes for regional catchment + festive + wedding-season campaigns. Native-speaker + culturally-accurate outperforms English-only by 25-40%. English-only only if targeting pure urban + high-income + young-professional.</p>
                                        <h3>Is Hyderabad a growing D2C skincare market?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes emerging. Growing tech + startup ecosystem + VC-backed D2C brands emerging (particularly ayurveda + wellness). Telugu + English + Hindi creative + Ugadi + Diwali + wedding-driven.</p>
                                        <h3>What ayurveda + heritage positioning works in South + East India?</h3>
                                        <p>South Indian temple + traditional herbal + Bengali traditional + regional heritage. Kama Ayurveda + Just Herbs + regional-heritage brands. Ingredient + heritage + storytelling-heavy positioning.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a realistic agency retainer for Chennai + Kolkata + Hyderabad?</h3>
                                        <p>Same tiered pricing as pan-India: Rs 65K-1.5L Starter, Rs 1.5-3.5L Growth, Rs 4L+ Enterprise. Regional-language creative may add 5-10%.</p>
                                        <h3>Does ITD handle regional-language creative?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes. Native-speaker Tamil + Malayalam + Bengali + Telugu writers + editors + video captioners on contract. Culturally-accurate messaging reviewed by regional strategists. Multilingual A/B testing on paid channels.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD support broader South + East India catchment?</h3>
